course: dictionary
lesson: 9078
title: Splash and slosh
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When a liquid sloshes, it moves about noisily and splashes inside its container or over the edge. Think of carrying a full bucket up the stairs: the water rocks from side to side and some of it spills out. «Slosh the water at one end of a full bath with your hand» and you can watch the wave move across the bath.
explain: Use the words around slosh to work out its meaning. «Gulping two whole bottles at once just sloshes about in your tummy.» Gulping, bottles and tummy tell you the drink is moving around inside, not sitting still. Sloshes about means moves around and splashes.
explain: Slosh is a sound word, so it helps the reader hear the scene. You can also slosh through water or mud: to walk with splashing steps. «Slosh through the puddles» is a phrase you might hear on a wet day, with wellies on.
fact: Slosh is a verb and a noun: you can slosh water, or you can have a slosh of juice in your cup.
fact: The verb forms are slosh, sloshes, sloshed and sloshing.
fact: «Sloshing» means moving noisily and splashing inside a container.
fact: To slosh through a puddle means to walk through it with splashing steps.
fact: In UK informal talk, «sloshed» means drunk, so do not use it for water in your writing.
exercise: «Gulping two whole bottles at once just sloshes about in your tummy.» What does sloshes about mean here? | *Moves around and splashes | Stays still and quiet | Tastes sweet | Turns into ice
exercise: Sam walks ___ the puddles with splashing steps. Which word fits the gap? | Stares | Floats | *sloshes | Tiptoes
exercise: Yesterday the bucket ___ over the edge when Ali ran up the stairs. Which word fits? | sloshing | slosh | *sloshed | sloshes
test: Which sentence uses slosh correctly? | The cake sloshes into the oven | The sun sloshes in the sky | Maya sloshes her homework neatly | *The bath water sloshed over the edge when Ben jumped in
test: Which phrase means to walk through water with splashing steps? | slosh in the sky | slosh about | slosh the sofa | *slosh through the puddles
exam: «Slosh the water at one end of a full bath with your hand.» What does slosh mean in this sentence? | Count the drops one by one | Heat it up until it steams | *Pour or splash it about | Freeze it into ice
